  "body": "Found by the review of #2490 (comment 6975287014). Refs #2473.\n\nFacts:\n- `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs:520` reads a move with no axis as \"keep the current angle\".\n- The Tormach post (`assets/posts/tormach.cps`) reads the first such move of a section as A0. The post states this turn with a Z lift. It is not silent.\n- Issue #2473 asks for a recorded `.cl` file. The file shows if the toolpath stream can produce a move with no A word in an indexed operation. PR #2490 gives a code reading. It gives no recording.\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:720-722`: arcs, cycles and probe moves with no A word now show the \"states no A angle\" message. No test pins the message of these record kinds.\n\nThe stream and the post read one record in two ways. A decision must pick one meaning.\n\nDone means:\n- One decision names the single meaning of a record with no axis.\n- A recorded `.cl` file, or a test, pins that the generators state the axis on each move of an indexed operation.\n- A test pins the refusal message for an arc, a cycle and a probe move with no A word.\n",
